  "limitations": [
    "Single-view TRELLIS reconstruction: fused 3-4 finger 'mitten' hands and a soft, low-detail face; mail rings, laces and buckles exist only as texture and baked normal relief.",
    "The back of the body is a projected rear-view concept blended into TRELLIS's texture at the sides; a thin dark strip remains where neither view reaches.",
    "Maps are cooked at 1024 px on the decimated TRELLIS atlas (57% coverage, about 2.7 texels per cm) and ship at 512 px (about 1.35 texels per cm), the finest level the game camera samples; the charts touch, so filtering can show faint seams. A fresh unwrap was tried and rejected: it covered only 37% of the texture.",
    "Roughness, metalness and the faction-dye mask are derived from colour inside declared regions, not measured PBR or hand-painted masks.",
    "TRELLIS's colours came out darker than the concept. The base colour is lifted after the cook (derive_tone_cook.py) by luma power 0.6, the calibration's floor (the Crown archer and captain and both factions' troops stop there too), which still leaves the soldier darker than its concept: about 104.8/255 mean luma in the game against 110.8/255 (84.7/255 before the lift).",
